{
  "_comment": [
    "The frozen SC-701a holdout corpus.",
    "",
    "SC-701a is a claim about a population, and a population assembled after",
    "the run it grades is a description of what the code already does. This",
    "file is that population, frozen in its own commit before the acceptance",
    "run that grades it and before any production change made in response to",
    "it. `frozen_at_commit` names that commit once it exists.",
    "",
    "Every entry is a QUALIFYING session: a decision or a standing instruction",
    "that is expressed and THEN acted on. Adversarial decline cases are",
    "deliberately absent \u2014 they live in feature005_semantic_signals.rs and",
    "must never occupy a slot in this denominator, because a scenario that is",
    "supposed to produce nothing cannot be evidence that something is",
    "produced.",
    "",
    "Each entry carries four things in order: a vocabulary path touched",
    "BEFORE the turn under test (which is what justifies the signal's two",
    "tokens), the real vendor field carrying the semantic text, the expected",
    "durable identity, and a post-signal action proving the decision or",
    "instruction was then acted on. The vocabulary seed and the action are",
    "different roles and are not interchangeable.",
    "",
    "The six instruction entries are three repeated (kind, subject, object)",
    "pairs across two sessions each, because R8 makes a standing convention",
    "rest on repetition. That is R8's existing rule, matched by the corpus",
    "rather than weakened to fit it.",
    "",
    "A vocabulary path is repository-relative and carries no `src/` prefix: the directory component is what ranks as the module and therefore as the subject, so a prefix would make every subject `src`."
  ],
  "version": 1,
  "criterion": "SC-701a, SC-701b",
  "frozen_at_commit": "recorded by the commit that adds this file; see git log",
  "frozen_on": "2026-09-06",
  "qualifying_sessions": 20,
  "minimum_durable_matches": 14,
  "population": "claude_code and codex only (FR-727e); OpenCode emits no semantic signals",
  "scenarios": [
    {
      "id": "d01-storage-postgresql",
      "vendor": "claude_code",
      "semantic_role": "assistant_message",
      "vocabulary_path": "storage/postgresql.rs",
      "transient_text": "we should use postgresql for storage",
      "expected": {
        "signal": "decision",
        "subject": "storage",
        "object": "postgresql",
        "verb": "adopt",
        "durable_type": "decision",
        "topic_key": "decision.storage",
        "value_key": "postgresql"
      },
      "post_signal_action": {
        "tool": "shell",
        "command": "cargo test -p postgresql"
      }
    },
